IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hbc-contracts`

-- Home Building Contracts Act 1991 (WA) -- worked cases, from the seat of the home owner contracting a builder.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case, a Building Commissioner decision or the Commissioner's guidance. The Home Building Contracts
-- Regulations 1992 (deposited) supply the thresholds ($7 500, $500 000, $20 000), the cabinetry deposit (20%), the
-- insurance amounts ($40 000, $200 000) and the excess ($500).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table (scratchpad gen_wa_home-building-contracts-act-1991_baseline.py). Expected results
-- were written by hand from the text.

`Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` MEANS Contract WITH
    `kind of work` IS `building or rebuilding a home`
    `is a cost plus contract` IS FALSE
    `is for a builder who must do the work under another contract` IS FALSE
    `amount stated as payable` IS 340000
    `estimated cost in the building permit application` IS 0
    `is in writing setting out all its terms` IS TRUE
    `shows the date of the contract` IS TRUE
    `is signed by the builder and by me` IS TRUE
    `I was given the notice before I signed` IS TRUE
    `deposit the contract lets the builder take` IS 22100
    `lets the builder take other payments before work starts` IS FALSE
    `lets the builder take payments after work starts that are not for work done or materials supplied` IS FALSE
    `is for cabinetry work, more than half of it off-site` IS FALSE
    `is headed and acknowledged as a cost plus contract` IS FALSE
    `number of homes in the contract` IS 1
    `needs a building permit` IS TRUE
    `is a prescribed building service` IS TRUE
    `falls in a Minister's insurance exemption period` IS FALSE

