§ `s 3 and r 2A -- which contracts the Act covers`

-- c051: $340,000 is more than $7,500 and less than $500,000 (r 2A).
#ASSERT `Is my contract a home building work contract` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract`
-- r 2A(a): $7,500 "or less" is out.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my contract a home building work contract` `a renovation at 7500`
-- r 2A(b): $500,000 "or more" is out.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my contract a home building work contract` `a build at 500000`

§ `s 4 and s 5 -- writing, signature, the notice, the copy`

-- c051
#ASSERT `Is my contract made as the Act requires` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract`
-- s 4(1)(b)
#ASSERT NOT `Is my contract made as the Act requires` `an unsigned build contract`
-- c051: s 4(3), r 3 and Schedule 1.
#ASSERT `Must I be given the notice before I sign` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract`
-- s 5(3)
#ASSERT `Within how many working days must the builder give me a copy` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS 10

§ `s 10 -- deposit and progress payments`

-- c051: 6.5% of $340,000 (s 10(1)(a)(i)).
#ASSERT `What is the most deposit my builder may take` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS 22100
-- r 3A(3): 20% of $30,000.
#ASSERT `What is the most deposit my builder may take` `a cabinetry contract at 30000 with a 20 per cent deposit` EQUALS 6000
-- c051: a $22,100 deposit is within the cap.
#ASSERT NOT `Do my contract's payment terms break the limits` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract`
-- $27,200 is over $22,100.
#ASSERT `Do my contract's payment terms break the limits` `a build contract with an 8 per cent deposit`
-- s 10(5): a genuine progress payment.
#ASSERT `May my builder demand this progress payment` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- s 10(5): neither for work done nor on the schedule.
#ASSERT NOT `May my builder demand this progress payment` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `ss 4(5), 10(4), 14, 19 -- ending the contract for the way it was made`

-- s 14(1)
#ASSERT `Is my cost plus contract missing its heading or acknowledgment` `a cost plus build at 300000 with no heading`
-- s 14(2): $500,000 or more is within para (b) of the definition, so s 14(1) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my cost plus contract missing its heading or acknowledgment` `a cost plus build at 600000 with no heading`
-- s 4(5), before completion (s 19(2)).
#ASSERT `May I terminate my contract for the way it was made` `an unsigned build contract` FALSE
-- s 19(2): the notice must come before completion.
#ASSERT NOT `May I terminate my contract for the way it was made` `an unsigned build contract` TRUE
-- s 4(5) reaches only s 4(1); missing the s 4(3) notice is not a ground.
#ASSERT NOT `May I terminate my contract for the way it was made` `a build contract with no notice given` FALSE
-- s 14(3)
#ASSERT `May I terminate my contract for the way it was made` `a cost plus build at 300000 with no heading` FALSE

§ `ss 7 and 8 -- variations`

-- s 8(1)(a), statement within 10 working days (s 8(2)).
#ASSERT NOT `Must the variation be in writing and signed by me` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` `a written direction under a written law` 5
-- s 8(2): the statement came too late.
#ASSERT `Must the variation be in writing and signed by me` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` `a written direction under a written law` 12
-- s 8(4): cost rises alone are not unforeseen.
#ASSERT `Must the variation be in writing and signed by me` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` `a rise in the builder's labour or material costs` 3
-- s 7(2)(b): no copy before the varied work began.
#ASSERT NOT `Was my variation made as the Act requires` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- s 8(3)
#ASSERT `Within how many working days must I dispute an unforeseen variation` `circumstances the builder could not reasonably have foreseen` EQUALS 10

§ `s 13 and Schedule 1 cl 4 -- the fixed price`

-- s 13(1)-(3): a rise-and-fall clause is void.
#ASSERT NOT `Can my builder raise my price` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` `a rise in labour or material costs` TRUE
-- s 13(4)(b)
#ASSERT `Can my builder raise my price` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` `a rise in a tax, duty or charge after the contract date` TRUE
-- c051 facts: over 5% of $340,000 ($17,000), within 10 working days.
#ASSERT `May I terminate because of the price rise` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` 17001 10 FALSE
-- cl 4(b): the increase must exceed 5%.
#ASSERT NOT `May I terminate because of the price rise` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` 17000 3 FALSE
-- cl 4(c)
#ASSERT `Must I pay the builder's reasonable costs` TRUE

§ `s 9 and Schedule 1 cll 1-3 -- the building permit condition`

-- Sch 1 cl 1
#ASSERT `What happens if the permit is late` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` `the builder alone` EQUALS `the contract stays in force on the same terms`
-- Sch 1 cl 2 and cl 4
#ASSERT `What happens if the permit is late` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` `me alone` EQUALS `the contract stays in force but the builder may raise the price by notice`
-- s 9(5)(b): associated work only.
#ASSERT `What happens if the permit is late` `a pool-only contract at 40000` `neither of us` EQUALS `the permit condition does not apply`

§ `s 11 -- defects`

-- notified in writing in the fourth month after practical completion.
#ASSERT `Must my builder make good this defect` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` 3 0 FALSE
-- outside the 4 months, and the contract gives no longer period.
#ASSERT NOT `Must my builder make good this defect` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` 4 0 FALSE

§ `ss 26 and 28`

-- s 26(2)(a)
#ASSERT `Is this inspection restriction binding` `only in the builder's normal working hours`
-- s 28(1), (2)
#ASSERT NOT `Does my waiver bind me` TRUE

§ `Part 3A -- home indemnity insurance`

-- s 25A para (b): the estimate in the permit application.
#ASSERT `What is the cost of my building work` `a cost plus build at 300000 with no heading` EQUALS 280000
-- r 7: $20,000 "or less" is out.
#ASSERT NOT `Is my work residential building work` `a renovation at 20000`
-- c051: ss 25B, 25C(1).
#ASSERT `Must my builder insure my work` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract`
-- s 25B(4A)(a)
#ASSERT NOT `Must my builder insure my work` `a kitchen renovation at 60000 needing no permit`
-- Part 3A has no upper limit: a $550,000 build is outside Part 2 but must still be insured.
#ASSERT `Must my builder insure my work` `the same build priced at 550000`
-- c051: s 25C(2).
#ASSERT `Must I get the insurance certificate before any payment` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract`
-- c051
#ASSERT `May my builder ask me for this deposit` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` 22100 TRUE
-- c051 facts without the certificate: s 25C(2).
#ASSERT NOT `May my builder ask me for this deposit` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` 22100 FALSE
-- c051: the lesser of $200,000 (r 7B) and $340,000.
#ASSERT `How much must the insurance cover me for` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS 200000
-- c051: under the $40,000 limit (r 7A).
#ASSERT `How much of my deposit is insured` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` 22100 EQUALS 22100
-- r 7A limit.
#ASSERT `How much of my deposit is insured` `the same build priced at 550000` 50000 EQUALS 40000
-- c051: s 25D(1)(d).
#ASSERT `For how many years can I claim on the insurance` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS 6
-- r 5
#ASSERT `What is the most excess on my claim` `Chloe and Liam's Byford building contract` EQUALS 500

§ `Disputes`

-- Notice for the Home Owner, Disputes 1.
#ASSERT `Within how many years must I complain` `a breach of the contract or of Part 2` EQUALS 3
